 "plentyVoiceSamples": [
  "d2: 🍽️ Theo counts the pantry jars twice, then sets down the gathering sack. \"We're eating well. Sharpening the skinning knives instead.\"",
  "d2: 🍽️ Hassan taps the pantry door — full to bursting — and keeps the day's share in hand. \"Dinner's on me tonight, then.\"",
  "d3: 🍽️ Theo taps the pantry's fullest jar. \"More than we can eat before it turns. Rendering fat instead — the lamps won't fill themselves.\"",
  "d3: 🍽️ Nino carries the day's surplus to the pantry door, thinks better of it, and turns back to the fire. \"It'll only rot in there. We eat.\"",
  "d6: 🍽️ Hassan weighs the day's basket against the pantry shelves and puts it down. \"Enough. Carving bowls instead — we're down to the cracked ones.\"",
  "d6: 🍽️ Blanca carries the day's surplus to the pantry door, thinks better of it, and turns back to the fire. \"It'll only rot in there. We eat.\"",
  "d7: 🍽️ Theo lingers by the full pantry and laughs. \"Full shelves, full bellies. Mending the palisade today — the fence won't fix itself.\"",
  "d7: 🍽️ Boris looks at the full shelves and waves off the day's share. \"No more into the store — we eat at the fire, and the shelves keep.\"",
  "d8: 🍽️ Nathan lingers by the full pantry and laughs. \"Full shelves, full bellies. Mending the palisade today — the fence won't fix itself.\"",
  "d8: 🍽️ Diana looks at the full shelves and waves off the day's share. \"No more into the store — we eat at the fire, and the shelves keep.\"",
  "d9: 🍽️ Blanca counts the pantry jars twice, then sets down the gathering sack. \"We're eating well. Sharpening the skinning knives instead.\"",
  "d9: 🍽️ Theo taps the pantry door — full to bursting — and keeps the day's share in hand. \"Dinner's on me tonight, then.\"",
  "d10: 🍽️ Diana stands in the pantry doorway a moment. \"Look at all this. Tending the fire today — someone ought to keep the stories.\"",
  "d10: 🍽️ Diana watches another basket arrive and laughs. \"We're feeding the shelves more than ourselves. Not today.\"",
  "d11: 🍽️ Nino lingers by the full pantry and laughs. \"Full shelves, full bellies. Mending the palisade today — the fence won't fix itself.\"",
